    <solution><m>\mathbf{(a)}</m> Since <m>r=3</m> and <m>\theta =\frac{\pi}{3}</m>, we have:
<me>x=r\cos\theta=3\cos \frac{\pi}{3}=3\cdot \frac12=1.5</me>
<me>y=r\sin\theta=3\sin \frac{\pi}{3}=3\cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}=2.59808</me>
<me>\Downarrow</me>
<me>(x,y)=(1.5,2.59808)</me>



<m>\mathbf{(b)}</m> For <m>(3,\frac{\pi}{2})</m> we have <m>r=3</m> and <m>\theta=\frac{\pi}{2}</m>. Hence,
<me>x=r\cos\theta=3\cos \frac{\pi}{2}=3\cdot 0=0</me>
<me>y=r\sin\theta=3\sin \frac{\pi}{2}=3\cdot 1=3</me>
<me>\Downarrow</me>
<me>(x,y)=(0,3)</me>



<m>\mathbf{(c)}</m> Since <m>r=6</m> and <m>\theta =\frac{\pi}{4}</m>, we have:
<me>x=r\cos\theta=6\cos \frac{\pi}{4}=6\cdot \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}=4.24264</me>
<me>y=r\sin\theta=6\sin \frac{\pi}{4}=6\cdot \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}=4.24264</me>
<me>\Downarrow</me>
<me>(x,y)=(4.24264,4.24264)</me>


</solution>
